From 5e447a6f9380329755e743c0fee57de26312a140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burnling <behld@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 02:39:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add LaneRobotV3B head and V3B training pipeline

Model: LaneRobotV3B head (per-lane classifiers shared across 56 rows, fixed bilinear row sampling, row mean + row embedding), output protocol unchanged [B,321,56,4]+[B,1,56,4]; backbone/neck identical to V2; new yolo26s-lane-v3b.yaml.

Input size changed: unified to 256x448 (previously 256x320 train / 320x320 deploy). H/W both divisible by 32, fused feat 16x28, aspect 1.75 close to native 16:9; training/export/deploy now use the same size.

Training: train_v3b.py is the V3B entry. Start: python train_v3b.py --weights <V2.pt> --name lane_v3b. --weights transfers backbone/neck (L0-L15), head starts random. Defaults: batch=-1, lr0=3e-4, epochs=500, patience=100, imgsz 256x448.

Loss/metrics/data: soft-label center and offset target both use round(target_x); validator reports per-lane MAE/Acc@1/3/5/Exist; dataset root overridable via LANE_ROBOT_DATASETS; default.yaml lane params aligned to V3B.

Before training, run a lightweight dataset EDA: per-slot presence rate and x distribution, lead_lane symmetry (fliplr safety), far-row density, label-image overlays, train/val overlap; use per-slot stats to decide no-lane bias init if needed.
